lines += ['', '## 3. Algorithms','', '### Tabular methods','', '**Q-Learning** is off-policy: it updates toward the largest next-state action value, irrespective of the next action actually sampled. **SARSA** is on-policy: its target uses the next action selected by the current epsilon-greedy policy. Both use α=0.15, γ=0.99, ε initially 1.0, decay 0.999 per episode to a floor of 0.03, and six action values per state. They provide the classical baselines and directly answer the assignment’s required comparison. Q-Learning can favor a greedy route despite exploratory behavior; SARSA accounts for the exploratory policy and may learn a more conservative route.','', '### Deep reinforcement learning methods','', '- **DQN:** a neural network estimates six action values; replay memory and a target network stabilize off-policy temporal-difference learning. Epsilon-greedy exploration is annealed during training.','- **PPO:** a categorical actor and value critic are trained on-policy; the clipped objective limits large policy changes.','- **A2C:** an actor chooses actions and a critic estimates values; advantage estimates guide synchronous on-policy updates.','', 'DQN, PPO, and A2C were selected because they represent value-based deep RL, clipped policy optimization, and advantage actor-critic, respectively. The comparison spans distinct learning objectives while keeping the discrete action interface unchanged. SB3 uses an MLP with two 64-unit hidden layers and CPU execution.','', '## 4. Experimental setup','', f'- **Software:** Python 3.12.2, Gymnasium 1.1.1, Stable-Baselines3 2.6.0, PyTorch 2.5.1, NumPy/pandas/matplotlib; CPU-compatible execution.','- **Training seeds:** 17, 29, 41 for every learned algorithm and board.','- **Budgets:** 3,500 episodes per tabular run; 6,000 environment timesteps per SB3 run.','- **Evaluation:** 100 separate episodes per final policy; SB3 checkpoint checks every 750 timesteps on 50 episodes; tabular checkpoint checks every 500 episodes on 100 episodes. Evaluation does not update policies.','- **Convergence rule:** three consecutive checkpoint evaluation windows each with at least 95% wins. Convergence episode is reported as the checkpoint where the third qualifying window ends. Otherwise it is “Not converged within training budget.”','- **Training time:** wall-clock seconds are reported per run in the CSV. Tabular budgets are episodes and DRL budgets are timesteps; these units are not interchangeable.','- **Baselines:** uniform random actions and an exact BFS shortest-path search over the known deterministic transition graph. BFS optimizes number of moves; the RL agents optimize cumulative reward.','', 'A deterministic learned policy on a fixed deterministic board produces the same path on every repeated evaluation episode. Therefore, 100 episodes do not imply 100 independent environment outcomes for a learned deterministic policy; variation across the three training seeds is the meaningful source of observed spread. Random-policy episodes use different action streams.','', '## 5. Results','', '### Final evaluation by board and algorithm','', 'Learned-agent values are mean ± sample standard deviation across three training seeds; Random is a single seeded baseline estimate. Success and reward are shown in percentage and reward units.','', '| Board | Algorithm | Success % | Moves | Cumulative reward | Training time (s) | Convergence episode by seed |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
lines += ['', '### DRL hyperparameters', '', '| Algorithm | Hyperparameters |', '|---|---|', '| DQN | learning rate 0.001; replay buffer 20,000; learning starts 500; batch 64; gamma 0.99; train frequency 4; target update 500; epsilon anneals to 0.05 over half the run |', '| PPO | learning rate 0.0003; rollout 256; batch 64; 5 epochs; gamma 0.99; GAE 0.95; entropy 0.01 |', '| A2C | learning rate 0.0007; rollout 16; gamma 0.99; GAE 0.95; entropy 0.01 |', '| All SB3 | MLP [64,64]; CPU; run-specific seed |', '']
