doc.add_paragraph('BFS shortest paths contain 3, 3, and 9 moves for the three layouts. Q-Learning and SARSA match the 3-move optimum on the first two boards. None of the learned methods won on the 100-square board during final evaluation at the stated budgets. BFS knows the full transition graph and directly optimizes shortest path; it is a strong and simpler solution for this deterministic known board. RL becomes relevant when the model is unknown, stochastic, dynamic, or when the objective differs from shortest path.')
doc.add_paragraph('Tabular methods achieved 100% measured success across seeds on the 30- and 50-square boards and checkpoint convergence at episode 1,500. DQN and A2C varied sharply by seed. PPO solved the 30-square board across seeds but did not solve the 50-square board in final evaluation. The 100-square failures demonstrate that the selected interaction budget was insufficient, not that learning is impossible. Snake and ladder placement affects route length and reward feedback, so board layout matters along with board size.')
doc.add_heading('6. Answers to assignment questions',1)
for q,a in answers:
    doc.add_heading(q,2); doc.add_paragraph(a)
doc.add_heading('7. Final experimental audit and 100-square improvement',1)
doc.add_paragraph(f'All {len(policy_audit)} original and {len(improved_policy_audit)} improved policy artifacts passed loading and structural checks. The original final summary reconciles to {int((reconciliation.status=="matched").sum())} independent saved-policy evaluation rows with no differences in reported success, moves, or cumulative reward. Final evaluation ran in fresh environments with no learning updates; checkpoint evaluations were read-only.')
doc.add_paragraph('The 10,000-episode random audit found one 400-step failure on the 100-square board. The earlier 100/100 success report was a finite sample, not a guarantee.')
t=doc.add_table(rows=1,cols=4);t.style='Light Shading Accent 1'
for c,v in zip(t.rows[0].cells,['Board','Success','Mean moves','Mean return']):c.text=v
for r in random_audit.itertuples():
    row=t.add_row().cells
    for c,v in zip(row,[r.board,f'{r.success_rate*100:.2f}%',fmt(r.avg_moves),fmt(r.avg_reward)]):c.text=v
doc.add_paragraph('Independent BFS reproduced shortest-path distances 3, 3, and 9 for the exact saved boards.')
doc.add_heading('Convergence and the SARSA 100-square result',2)
doc.add_paragraph('The stored convergence episode is the first point with three consecutive validation windows at or above 95%; it does not enforce retention through final evaluation. SARSA seeds 17, 29, and 41 all first crossed this threshold at episode 1,500, but all final policies were at 0%. For seed 17, validation success stayed at 100% through episode 2,500, then fell to 0% at episodes 3,000 and 3,500. The original convergence column is therefore a transient threshold crossing, not durable convergence. The audit CSV records both measures.')
doc.add_heading('Longer budget at gamma 0.99',2)
doc.add_paragraph('The original experiment files remain unchanged. New seeds 71, 83, and 97 were trained on the same board and reward function for 20,000 tabular episodes or 25,000 SB3 timesteps, with a slower tabular epsilon schedule and adjusted DRL hyperparameters. All 15 final policies still had 0% success and 400 mean moves.')
t=doc.add_table(rows=1,cols=5);t.style='Light Shading Accent 1'
for c,v in zip(t.rows[0].cells,['Algorithm','Success %','Mean moves','Mean return','Budget']):c.text=v
for algo in ['q_learning','sarsa','DQN','PPO','A2C']:
    g=improved[improved.algorithm==algo]; budget='20,000 episodes' if algo in ('q_learning','sarsa') else '25,000 steps'
    row=t.add_row().cells
    for c,v in zip(row,[algo,mean_sd(g,'success_rate',100),mean_sd(g,'avg_moves'),mean_sd(g,'avg_reward'),budget]):c.text=v
doc.add_heading('Separate discount-factor sweep',2)
doc.add_paragraph('Per-step reward values were unchanged. At alpha 0.10, epsilon 1.0 decaying by 0.9998 to 0.02, and 20,000 episodes, gamma 0.80 and 0.90 produced 100% final success for Q-Learning and SARSA at both tested seeds (71 and 97). Every winning policy averaged 10 moves and cumulative reward 196, one move above BFS.')
t=doc.add_table(rows=1,cols=5);t.style='Light Shading Accent 1'
for c,v in zip(t.rows[0].cells,['Algorithm','Gamma','Seeds','Success %','Moves / return']):c.text=v
for (algo,gam),g in gamma.groupby(['algorithm','gamma']):
    row=t.add_row().cells
    for c,v in zip(row,[algo,f'{gam:.2f}','71, 97',mean_sd(g,'success_rate',100),f'{g.avg_moves.mean():.0f} / {g.avg_reward.mean():.0f}']):c.text=v
doc.add_paragraph('The gamma 0.99 histories also contained successful earlier checkpoints. Four were replayed, saved separately, and each won on its held-out deterministic policy rollouts. Their files are under models/improved/checkpoint_selected/.')
doc.add_heading('Reward-loop diagnosis',2)
doc.add_paragraph('Greedy traces found repeated-state loops. One improved SARSA loop collected +38 undiscounted reward over six transitions and a Q-Learning loop collected +14 over nine. Original tabular policies also repeated overshoot at square 95. The +20 ladder reward can make cycle return compete with reaching the goal; truncation adds no failure penalty. Lower gamma reduced the value of delayed cycle rewards in this test while preserving each transition reward.')
for name,caption in [('original_vs_improved_success.png','Original vs longer-budget and gamma-sweep success rates.'),('original_vs_improved_moves.png','Mean moves, with failures counted at the 400-step cap; logarithmic scale.'),('gamma_sweep_learning.png','Separate validation success during the discount-factor sweep.')]:
    p=doc.add_paragraph();p.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER;p.add_run().add_picture(str(ROOT/'results'/'improved'/'plots'/name),width=Inches(6.1))
    q=doc.add_paragraph(caption);q.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER
doc.add_heading('8. Limitations and future work',1)
doc.add_paragraph('The improvement test covers one fixed 100-square layout and two seeds per gamma value. DQN, PPO, and A2C did not improve success within the tested 25,000-timestep budget. Further work should evaluate more independent layouts and longer DRL budgets, and can explore stochastic/dynamic variants. Original experiment results and policies remain preserved.')
doc.add_heading('9. Conclusion',1)
doc.add_paragraph('The audit verified all 45 original policies, reconciled the saved-policy evaluations, and independently confirmed BFS. Longer training at gamma 0.99 did not improve board 3 success. A separate unchanged-reward discount sweep produced Q-Learning and SARSA policies that win in 10 moves, close to BFS’s 9. The audit also identified transient convergence and repeat-state reward cycles.')
